If a Suricata engine binary is not already present, build one from `/app` into `/app/src/suricata`. Run it over `/data/pcaps/session.pcap` with your config so `/results/eve.json` is created (JSON lines). Then write `/results/audit-summary.json` with exactly these keys: `http_rule_count` (integer, number of `alert` rules in `/results/http-events.rules`), `tls_rule_count` (integer, number of `alert` rules in `/results/tls-events.rules`), `eve_records` (integer, number of JSON lines in `/results/eve.json`, must be >= 1), `eve_http_events` (integer, count of eve records whose `event_type` is `http`), `eve_tls_events` (integer, count whose `event_type` is `tls`), `eve_alert_events` (integer, count whose `event_type` is `alert`), `tls_extended_fields_present` (boolean, true if at least one tls eve record includes a `tls` object with a `sni` or `version` or `subject` field; must be true), `rules_load_ok` (boolean, true if the engine run exited 0; must be true). Trailing newline required.
